{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROOT CAUSE FOUND for the 2026-08-07 status reversion on this ticket. Filed as bug\n`e6e9-ddbf-223b-4f49` (coal-semiliquid-heifer), linked `discovered_from` 4136. Summary here so\nthe trail survives on the ticket that showed the symptom.\n\n**The projection is NOT at fault.** The reconciler event is genuinely the latest status event in\nthis ticket's log:\n`1786097878273766164-d80fab3f-4d15-404c-9b20-ef7ec4fbeb27-STATUS.json`,\n`{\"author\":\"reconciler\",\"env_id\":\"reconciler\",\"data\":{\"current_status\":\"open\",\"status\":\"closed\"}}`.\nAn inbound pass wrote it. This is not a replay or compaction defect.\n\n**Mechanism.** ADR 0026 Decision 1 makes the per-binding baseline the only direction signal:\n`local == baseline` is read as \"local did not change, so a differing Jira value must be a\nJira-side edit — suppress the outbound push and let inbound mirror it\"\n(`outbound_field_diff.py:323-334`, status branch `:389-396`). Inbound has no arbitration of its\nown (`inbound_differ.py:233-234`) and can only clobber a field in a pass where outbound emitted\nnothing for it (`inbound_differ.py:709-718`).\n\nThe baseline is advanced from the pass-START snapshot (`reconcile.py:595` ->\n`_advance_baselines`, `reconcile.py:514-531`, using `ctx.curr_snapshot` fetched at\n`reconcile.py:280` BEFORE the outbound apply). So in the pass where rebar itself pushes a status\nto Jira, the baseline keeps the OLD value for one pass. A REOPEN is a revert to a previous\nvalue, so it lands exactly in that window:\n\n1. Pass N (run 31168795002) pushed the close: `RECON: outbound_update key=REB-2500\n   changed=[description,status]`. Jira became `Done`. Baseline NOT advanced — bindings.json at\n   f0fe2ce9d4 (10:14:45Z) still records `baseline.status = 'To Do'`.\n2. The reopen at 10:09:14Z set local back to `open`.\n3. Pass N+1 (run 31169292024): local `open` == canonicalized baseline `To Do` -> `open`, so\n   status was suppressed outbound: `RECON: outbound_update key=REB-2500 changed=[description]`.\n   Inbound then read Jira's `Done` and overwrote local. Clobber at 10:17:58Z.\n\n**Why the description survived and the status did not.** Description differed from the stale\nbaseline, so it was pushed and inbound had nothing to say. Status equalled the stale baseline, so\noutbound stood down and inbound won. The asymmetry falls straight out of the guard.\n\n**Discriminating experiment.** Replaying the real pass-time inputs through\n`outbound_field_diff.compute_update_fields` with the baseline as the only variable:\n\n    STALE baseline 'To Do' (the real pass-time value)\n       -> outbound fields = {'description': 'NEW'}                     status_sent=False\n    ADVANCED baseline 'Done' (what outbound had just pushed)\n       -> outbound fields = {'description': 'NEW', 'status': 'To Do'}  status_sent=True\n\nThe stale row reproduces the observed `changed=[description]` exactly.\n\n**Not a regression from today's work.** The clobbering pass started 10:14:54Z; every suspect\ncommit landed later (e7a9 12:16Z, 851e 12:25Z, 2876 12:34Z, 65d7 13:13Z). The same shape also\noccurred on 2026-07-20 across 8 tickets. Pre-existing; surfaced today only because the Reconcile\nBridge was re-enabled mid-session.\n\n**Current risk.** Self-limiting: after the clobber the baseline advances to Jira's value, local\nthen differs from it, and the next pass pushes local out. Both this ticket and 556a have\nconverged and are holding `open`. No bridge pause is needed, but any future reopen made within\none pass of rebar's own status push can be clobbered once."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786122327327506001,"uuid":"28103950-aa1a-48bb-9f95-b6f0038931d7"}